summary:
## Current Focus

Polishing the Fatlind Azemi portfolio to ultra-premium agency tier. Fixing visual harmony: card spacing/contrast, integrating the real profile photo, removing the top navbar (keeping sidebar dots), trimming tag overflow, and verifying the final look via screenshots.

## Environment

- **Stack**: Next.js 16.2.9 (Turbopack), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4
- **3D**: Three.js + @react-three/fiber + @react-three/postprocessing (Bloom)
- **Motion**: Framer Motion (Z-axis reveals, 3D card tilt, staggered children)
- **Project root**: `/Users/fatlind/Projekte/data-engineer-portfolio`
- **Profile image**: copied from `/Users/fatlind/Documents/bewerbung/Bild.png` → `public/profile.png`

## Completed Tasks

- **Global refactor**: Rebuilt all sections (Hero, About, Experience, Skills, Certs, Contact)
- **ZReveal system**: Replaced Y-axis slides with `opacity + scale + translateZ + blur` spatial reveals
- **GlassCard component**: Ultra-thin borders, `backdrop-blur(32px)`, inner protective slate-950 tint, 3D hover tilt, edge glow accent
- **SVG accents**: `SketchFrame` (self-drawing corner brackets) and `DataLine` (glowing data line with traveling packets)
- **Nav**: Removed top `Header`, kept `SideDots` sidebar navigation per user request
- **Spacing**: Increased grid gaps (`gap-7 md:gap-8` to `gap-8 md:gap-10`) and inner padding (`p-8 md:p-10` to `p-9 md:p-12`) across all cards
- **Tag trimming**: Reduced skill/experience tags to prevent overflow and visual clutter
- **Profile photo**: Integrated real image into About card with gradient overlay
- **Build/lint**: Passes cleanly (static prerender)

## Active Issues

- **Profile photo rendering**: `next/Image` with `fill` failed to render in headless screenshots; reverted to plain `<img>` with `object-cover` to guarantee visibility
- **Final verification**: Need to review latest screenshots after spacing/tag trims to confirm polished look
- **Dev overlay**: Next.js "4 Issues" badge visible only in dev mode, not production

## Code State

### `components/GlassCard.tsx`

Core glass surface with 3D tilt and protective inner layer.

```tsx
export default function GlassCard({ children, className, accentColor, hover3d = true }) {
  const cardRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const [transform, setTransform] = useState("perspective(1200px) rotateX(0) rotateY(0) scale3d(1,1,1)");
  // mouse-driven tilt ±6deg, edge glow via CSS --accent variable
  return (
    <div ref={cardRef} className={`glass-card ${className}`} style={{ transform, ["--accent" as any]: accentColor }}>
      <div className="card-glow" />
      <div className="card-content">{children}</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### `components/ZReveal.tsx`

Spatial entrance animation (emerges from particle space, no Y-slide).

```tsx
export default function ZReveal({ children, className, delay = 0, staggerChildren = false }) {
  const MotionTag = motion.div;
  if (staggerChildren) {
    return <MotionTag className={className} initial="hidden" whileInView="visible" viewport={{ once: true, amount: 0.25 }}
      variants={{ hidden: {}, visible: { transition: { staggerChildren: 0.12, delayChildren: delay } } }}>
      {children}
    </MotionTag>;
  }
  return <MotionTag className={className} initial={{ opacity: 0, scale: 0.92, z: -60, filter: "blur(8px)" }}
    whileInView={{ opacity: 1, scale: 1, z: 0, filter: "blur(0px)" }} viewport={{ once: true, amount: 0.25 }}
    transition={{ duration: 0.8, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] as const, delay }}>{children}</MotionTag>;
}
```

### `app/globals.css` (glass system)

```css
.glass-card {
  position: relative;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10);
  border-radius: 1.75rem;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  backdrop-filter: blur(32px);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.07), 0 24px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
}
.glass-card::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit;
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.68), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.46));
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 0;
}
.glass-card:hover {
  border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
}
.card-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
```

### `app/page.tsx`

- Removed `Header` component entirely
- Kept `SideDots` as sole navigation
- Structure: `ScrollProgress`, `CursorSpotlight`, `SideDots`, `PortfolioCanvas`, section stack

### `components/sections/AboutSection.tsx`

- Profile card uses real image `/profile.png` with gradient overlay
- Floating accent icons (Cloud/Award) made smaller and lower opacity
- Milestone stats use `ZRevealItem` stagger with `gap-5 md:gap-6`

### `components/sections/ExperienceSection.tsx`

- Metrics: `4+`, `Azure`, `GCP`, `2x` with short labels (`Jahre Erfahrung`, `Cloud`, `Zertifiziert`)
- Featured role tags trimmed to 4 core items
- Main/secondary cards use generous padding (`p-8 md:p-12 lg:p-14`)

### `components/sections/SkillsSection.tsx`

- Main cards trimmed to 5 tags each; secondary to 4–6 tags
- Grid gaps increased to `gap-8 md:gap-10` for main row

### `components/sections/CertsSection.tsx`

- Digital certificate cards with brand-colored glowing badge and `SketchFrame` corner accent
- Grid gap `gap-8 md:gap-10`

## Important Context

- **Design principle**: UI must emerge from the 3D particle space, not slide up. All reveals use Z-depth + opacity + scale.
- **Contrast guardrail**: Every card has an inner `::before` smoky tint so background neon/torus blur out softly while text stays sharp.
- **Button style**: No solid white blocks. Primary/outline buttons use `.btn-glow` with fine borders and radial hover glow.
- **Screenshot workflow**: Verified via Playwright + headless Chrome on `localhost:3001` after each polish pass.
- **User explicitly requested**: Keep sidebar dots, remove top nav, make it "very beautiful and highly modern".

## TODO List
  [in_progress] Integrate real profile photo into About section
  [pending] Polish Experience metrics and card spacing
  [pending] Trim/resize skill tags to prevent overflow
  [pending] Refine global glass styling and section breathing room
  [pending] Build, screenshot, and verify final look

